5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"Since we have more residents than spaces, we need a fair system. I suggest we look into the actual usage and the physical layout first. I'll check the sticker register and the rain exposure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree that fairness is key, but we also need to understand the financial side of this. I'll look into the building account's two-year ledger and the treasurer's handover file on cash collections.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,I believe we should verify if the current allocation is actually balanced. I will look into the sticker register and the daily riders to see who is truly using the spaces.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I'm less interested in the numbers and more in the human element. I'll check the five years of association minutes and last year's complaint log entries to see where we've failed before.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Mio,,I want to know how much work this actually takes to manage! I'll check the treasurer's handover file on cash collections and the account from the neighbouring block's secretary to see how others do it.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we have a good spread of data. @Ryuji and @Mio are focusing on finances, while @Shunichi is looking at history. I believe understanding the physical constraints is just as vital for a sustainable solution.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Mio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Physical constraints are important, but without knowing the budget or current revenue, we might propose something we can't afford to maintain. I want to ensure our final decision is financially grounded.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"Financials are necessary, but we must first ensure the current distribution isn't biased. I'll also look into the morning departures watched from the entrance to see the actual flow of residents.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, watching people leave in the morning sounds like a bit of a hobby, doesn't it? I'll stick to the records. It's far more efficient to see where people actually clashed than to guess from a distance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, don't be so grumpy! Watching people can be fun! But I agree that we need a plan that doesn't just look good on paper, but is actually easy for us to keep up!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@George, observing the morning flow is actually a logical step to identify congestion. I believe combining that with the rain exposure data will help us determine if some spaces are practically unusable.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"While observing flow is useful, we must not overlook the cost of implementing changes. If we decide to reorganize the layout, we need to know if there are funds available for new markings or signage.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,"I appreciate the support, @Asuka. I simply want to ensure that our decisions are based on reality rather than assumptions. I believe seeing the actual movement will clarify if the current layout is truly functional.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you're obsessing over signage costs for a few lines of paint. Let's focus on the social friction. If we ignore the history of complaints, we're just designing a new way for neighbors to hate each other.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, that's a bit dramatic! But you're right that we don't want more fighting. I just hope we don't create a system that's so complicated that whoever manages it just gives up!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"To wrap up this round, I will stick with the sticker register and rain exposure. It is essential to know who is actually using the spaces and which ones are physically problematic before we vote.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will stick with the building account's two-year ledger and the treasurer's handover file. We cannot make a responsible decision without knowing the actual financial impact and current collection status.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,"I will stick with the sticker register and the daily riders, and the morning departures. It is important to verify the actual usage patterns to ensure the allocation is truly fair and based on reality.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll stick with the five years of association minutes and last year's complaint log. Let's see if we can avoid repeating the same mistakes that turned this place into a battlefield.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Mio,,I'll stick with the treasurer's handover file and the account from the neighbouring block's secretary! I really want to see how much paperwork is involved so we don't accidentally create a nightmare job for someone!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
